				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/flamingzealot" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4922127); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4922127&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608567377" alt="flamingZealot" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4922127)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/flamingzealot" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4922127); return false;" >flamingZealot</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608164289 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Dec 2020 00:18</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846584">
									

<p>A coven of sirens- yes, like the mythological Greek kind- find themselves adapting to the modern climate in order to seek their prey.</p>
<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up extra space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) and titles short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights</strong>: Yes!</p>
<p><strong>Page Type</strong>: SCP Article.</p>
<p><strong>Genre</strong>: Comedy, mainly, but not in an un-serious manner.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>: You know those clearly fake ads you get on nsfw websites? The ones that’re like “HOT SINGLES IN YOUR AREA”, et cetera. Yeah. Those, but anomalous, and set up by Sirens, as in the type that’d lure sailors to death. The ad, if loaded on a page, would display a message along the lines of “10 HOT (xyz) WITHIN (distance)! TEXT NOW!”</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>As time went by, the distance would gradually decrease, and the number increase. This would culminate in the subject being ambushed, and then&#8230; well, consumed, by a number of horrible, vaguely humanoid mermaid-looking people. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">The tails are dorsal fins from catfishes.</span></p>
<p>The Foundation would later track these ads to a certain location, and, unable to block the ads via webcrawlers or other non-anomalous means, would send in an MTF team to find out what’s going on. There’s an exploration log- which I've always wanted to write, they're fun- and the anomaly is accidentally neutralised when the coven of sirens panics upon realising there’s angry fellows with guns in the hideout and collapses the building in order to escape, breaking the devices and thaumaturgy they're using to make the ads anomalous.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong>: The context behind this strange new manner of Greek monsters luring in prey is simply that people don’t usually fall for the ole’ “Sing to the sailors until they follow you and drown” trick, and they’ve had to resort to new and unusual means of tracking targets. Inkeeping with the tradition of luring sailors in with beautiful songs and false faces, they decide to essentially hijack NSFW spam ads.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber</strong>: As far as I’m aware, nobody’s done sirens as an SCP before, and beyond that, the concept of the fake ads on the sides of sketchy sites actually being dangerous beyond just giving your computer malware is a little spine-chilling. And also really funny, when you think about it.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes</strong>: As this would be my first SCP, essentially any critique at all would be greatly appreciated.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Edit 1: Paratech has been removed, at the advice of <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6846344&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608239079" alt="JamaisJ" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6846344)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;">JamaisJ</a></span>, and the idea of them being <em>literal</em> catfish mermaids was inspired by someone on IRC.</p>
<p><em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts and properly space your paragraphs. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p><em><sub>oops. thanks for the fixes- i’ll keep those in mind for the future ~zeal</sub></em></p>

